usage: profile_constrained.py [-h] --binary BINARY --code-model CODE_MODEL
                              --documents-model DOCUMENTS_MODEL --root ROOT
                              --protocol PROTOCOL --output OUTPUT

Actual-model Linux resident retrieval under explicit CPU/address limits.
Virtual address limits are not physical RAM, and CPU affinity does not emulate
a different processor. Preserve failed limits; only successful runs receive
exact output-equivalence credit. The protocol must exist before execution.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --binary BINARY
  --code-model CODE_MODEL
  --documents-model DOCUMENTS_MODEL
  --root ROOT
  --protocol PROTOCOL
  --output OUTPUT
